<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Caste War of Yucatán</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1847">1847</a>–<a href="/years/1901">1901</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caste">Caste</a> War of Yucatán was a long uprising of the Maya against the Hispanic and mestizo elites of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yucatan-peninsula">Yucatán Peninsula</a>. Beginning at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tepich">Tepich</a> in 1847, it nearly drove the whites to Mérida and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/campeche">Campeche</a>, forcing Yucatán to rejoin <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> in 1848. Rebel Maya then held the south-east from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/felipe-carrillo-puerto-quintana-roo">Chan Santa Cruz</a> for decades, and many refugees fled to British Honduras.</p></div>
